p6. Two objects, one word.

committed carrier files read: 6
regions: ['16384', '131072', '1048576', '2097152', '4194304', '8388608']
arms:    ['bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d64', 'bitpack-carrier-packed', 'bitpack-carrier-packed-simd']

=== object one: the SUPPORT, a set of demanded coordinates ===

generators: ['time', 'size']
non-empty subsets (the carrier of the free join semilattice): 3
ordered pairs: 9
pairs with a unique least upper bound under union: 9
join is total and canonical: True

So `106` section 5 is right ABOUT THIS OBJECT. Two strategies demanding
different coordinates combine into the one demanding both, uniquely.

=== object two: the RATE, a ray in the positive orthant ===

Two strategies with the SAME support {time, size} and different rates.
Four ordinary ways to combine two rays, all of them defensible, and the
section each selects on the committed table:

  arithmetic mean                              -> ('bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')
  componentwise max                            -> ('bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')
  componentwise min                            -> ('bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')
  geometric mean (squared, order preserving)   -> ('bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')
  first operand                                -> ('bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d32', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')
  second operand                               -> ('bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16', 'bitpack-carrier-d16')

distinct sections reached by six defensible combinations: 2

So `106` section 1 clause seven is right ABOUT THIS OBJECT. There is no
canonical combination of two rates: the ordinary candidates disagree on
the committed table, so a design that picks one has made a choice rather
than computed a join.

=== the same question over a grid of rate pairs ===

One pair refutes a canonical join. A rate of disagreement makes the
finding usable, so the six combinations are compared over every ordered
pair drawn from a log-spaced grid of exchange rates.

  ordered rate pairs swept:                       42
  pairs where the six combinations DISAGREE:      30 (71.4%)
  most distinct sections reached by one pair:     3

  holds for: regions = 6, arms = 5, cost coordinates = 2 (median algo_ns
  per record, declared bits per element as 16/32/64/13/13), cost source =
  the committed bitpack-carrier-width_n* CSVs, arithmetic exact rational,
  threads = 1, target features any

=== what the collision costs ===

The canon candidate's definition says two strategies are related by
nothing on their second component. Its own section 5 says the join on the
second component is union and free. A reader who takes the first cannot
build `97`'s demand lattice; a reader who takes the second will try to
join two exchange rates and find no least upper bound.

The repair is to split the word rather than to choose a side:

  component two = a SUPPORT (which coordinates are demanded) together
                  with a RATE (the exchange among them).

  supports join, uniquely and totally, by union. That is `97`'s lattice,
  it is compiled, and it is what makes silence a first-class element.

  rates do not join, and nothing should ask them to. Where two rates meet,
  either the site names one or the operation reports, exactly as clause
  seven says for the first component.

That also explains a result the unit has and does not connect: `93`'s four
markers leaving 12 of 16 ordered pairs unresolvable. The supports resolve
in all 16. What does not resolve is the rate, and a flat marker set was
carrying both in one slot, which is `94`'s own diagnosis of the flat set.
